Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.980
Speaker 1: There was a new CPAC straw poll
done this weekend at CPAC, and although Donald

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:12.430
Trump is still leading the 2024 presidential
straw poll.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:20.110
Ron DeSantis is polling higher than ever before
28 percent and Trump is furious.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:26.899
So we want to kind of consider this story
in the right context.

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:32.720
Trump is still winning the straw poll, but
the margin by which he is winning it for the

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.410
2024 Republican primary is as small as it
has ever been.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:44.480
The Hill reporting Trump wins CPAC straw poll
As the Santos's support grows, former President

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.829
Trump emerged as the clear winner.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:55.600
But Ron DeSantis is now up to 28 percent recall,
as the article does, that in last year's straw

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.600
poll.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.510
DeSantis had 21 percent support.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:08.310
In third place was Trump's former Secretary
of State Mike Pompeo, with two percent support.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:14.720
So Trump has been furious about what's going
on with the scientists for a long time now.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.630
You might remember that in November, I reported
to you, Trump's ire grows as DeSantis.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.830
His popularity with Republicans takes off,
and at that point, DeSantis was only polling

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.940
between 10 and 20 for the 2024 Republican
primary debate.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:36.409
Sending which poll you looked at and what's
at issue here and what Trump is so enraged

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:43.369
by is that a number of times now when DeSantis
has been asked Do you rule out running for

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:50.610
president in general or do you rule out running
if Trump runs and DeSantis has not ruled out

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.770
either?

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:58.320
And why would he, when you're polling 28 percent
and it's years from the election and you haven't

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:03.530
even really talked about running, you genuinely
have a good shot at being the Republican nominee.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:09.159
DeSantis would be crazy if he has any even
possibility of ambitions to be the Republican

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:10.159
nominee in 2024.

00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:13.239
DeSantis would be crazy to rule it out, so
of course he hasn't.

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:19.359
And Trump's furious since then, Trump has
gone at DeSantis, and DeSantis has also gone

00:02:19.359 --> 00:02:23.680
after Trump, saying things like, for example,
DeSantis.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.709
I don't know that I should have aligned myself
so closely with Trump early in the pandemic

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:30.370
might have not been the right decision.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:35.730
Trump going back at the Santas, the order
doesn't matter, but going at each other, saying,

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.469
you know, he's ungrateful, and he didn't really
even do that great of a job with the pandemic

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:41.549
or whatever the case may be.

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:48.999
And one great way to trigger Donald Trump
is to not be 100 percent subservient in every

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:50.639
single way.

00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:56.370
And Don Ron DeSantis, I've said before, I
believe Ron DeSantis is sort of like a more

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:04.749
dangerous version of Donald Trump in the sense
that it's the same wacky right wing ism completely

00:03:04.749 --> 00:03:09.010
disconnected from reality, facts, empiricism,
etc..

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.249
But DeSantis is slightly less cartoonish than
Trump.

00:03:12.249 --> 00:03:13.249
He's still a cartoon.

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:19.419
I mean, compared to, you know, old school
Republicans, DeSantis is still a total cartoon,

00:03:19.419 --> 00:03:21.510
but he is more competent.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:27.819
He's less obviously clueless, and he might
be more able to actually get things done in

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:30.919
the sort of Trumpian vein, and that makes
him a very dangerous guy.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:37.219
So are the the prospects for the country are,
of course, concerning in the sense that when

00:03:37.219 --> 00:03:45.939
a governor with endless unnecessary COVID
deaths is seeing his popularity take off,

00:03:45.939 --> 00:03:49.309
that should raise a red flag for all of us.

00:03:49.309 --> 00:03:57.400
At the same time, we saw 70 million people
vote for the completely moronic Donald Trump,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.439
who has even more deaths than that on his
hands with his sheer incompetence on the pandemic.

00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:05.559
And so it's been a serious problem for a while.

00:04:05.559 --> 00:04:11.870
I do think that one of the best possible scenarios
for the left and for the Democratic Party

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:18.019
because the left in the Democratic Party are
really not indicating to me that they have

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:24.260
